*==============================================================================
* IRLZ44N  -  N-Channel Power MOSFET  (TO-220AB)
* Infineon Technologies (International Rectifier)
*
* SPICE Level-3 Model
*
* Source:  Infineon IRLZ44N Datasheet
*          https://www.infineon.com/assets/row/public/documents/24/49/
*          infineon-irlz44n-datasheet-en.pdf
*
* Key Electrical Characteristics (from datasheet):
* -------------------------------------------------------
*  Parameter         Symbol    Value     Conditions
* -------------------------------------------------------
*  Drain-Source Volt  VDSS      55 V
*  Gate-Source Volt   VGSS     ±20 V
*  Drain Current      ID        47 A      Tc = 25°C (continuous)
*  Drain Current      ID        30 A      Tc = 100°C
*  Pulsed Drain Curr  IDM      160 A
*  Power Dissipation  PD       110 W      Tc = 25°C
*  Gate Threshold     VGS(th)   1.0–2.0V  (typ 1.5V) logic-level
*  On Resistance      RDS(on)  22 mΩ      VGS=10V, ID=41A
*  On Resistance      RDS(on)  25 mΩ      VGS=4.5V, ID=30A (typ)
*  Transconductance   gfs       40 S      VDS=25V, ID=20A
*  Input Capacitance  Ciss    2700 pF     VGS=0V, VDS=25V, f=1MHz
*  Output Capacitance Coss     810 pF     VGS=0V, VDS=25V, f=1MHz
*  Reverse Trans Cap  Crss     195 pF     VGS=0V, VDS=25V, f=1MHz
*  Total Gate Charge  QG        63 nC     VGS=10V, VDS=44V, ID=25A
*  Gate-Source Charge QGS       15 nC
*  Gate-Drain Charge  QGD       30 nC
*  Turn-On Delay      td(on)    27 ns     VDD=44V, ID=25A
*  Rise Time          tr        42 ns
*  Turn-Off Delay     td(off)   94 ns
*  Fall Time          tf        51 ns
*  Body Diode Current IS        47 A
*  Body Diode Vf      VSD        1.5 V    TJ=25°C, IS=25A, VGS=0V
*  Reverse Recovery   trr       136 ns    TJ=25°C, IF=25A, di/dt=100A/µs
*  Avalanche Energy   EAS       250 mJ    ID=47A
*  Thermal Res J-C    RθJC       0.80 °C/W
*  Thermal Res J-A    RθJA       62   °C/W (PCB mounted)
* -------------------------------------------------------
*
* SPICE Model Pin Order:  Drain  Gate  Source
*==============================================================================

.SUBCKT IRLZ44N  Drain  Gate  Source

* --- Internal nodes ---
* Rd  : drain bulk resistance
* Rs  : source bulk resistance
* Rg  : gate resistance
* M1  : intrinsic MOSFET
* Dbody : body (anti-parallel) diode

* Gate resistance (internal polysilicon + bond wire)
Rg    Gate  Gi    1.5

* Drain lead/bulk resistance
Rd    Drain  Di    0.8m

* Source lead/bulk resistance
Rs    Source  Si   0.5m

* ---------------------------------------------------------------
* Level-3 MOSFET — parameters derived from datasheet curves
*
*   VTO   = threshold voltage                 1.5 V
*   KP    = transconductance coefficient      derived from gfs=40S
*   GAMMA = bulk threshold modulation         0.1
*   PHI   = surface potential                 0.8 V
*   LAMBDA= channel length modulation         0.05 V⁻¹ (output slope)
*   RD/RS = zero (handled by external R above)
*   CGSO  = gate-source overlap cap           (Ciss-Crss) / W → scaled
*   CGDO  = gate-drain overlap cap            Crss / W → scaled
*   IS    = body diode saturation current
*   LEVEL = 3
*
* W and L are normalised; KP is adjusted so that
*   ID ≈ 47A at VGS=10V, VDS=10V, and
*   RDS(on) = VDS/ID ≈ 22mΩ in the linear region.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------

M1  Di  Gi  Si  Si  IRLZ44N_MOSFET  W=1  L=1u

.MODEL IRLZ44N_MOSFET  NMOS  LEVEL=3
+   VTO     = 1.5        $ Gate threshold voltage (V)
+   KP      = 62         $ Transconductance parameter (A/V²) — tuned for gfs=40S
+   GAMMA   = 0.1        $ Bulk threshold modulation (V^0.5)
+   PHI     = 0.8        $ Surface potential (V)
+   LAMBDA  = 0.05       $ Channel-length modulation (V⁻¹)
+   THETA   = 0.08       $ Mobility modulation (V⁻¹), limits gm at high VGS
+   KAPPA   = 1.0        $ Saturation field factor
+   ETA     = 0.0        $ Static feedback
+   VMAX    = 0          $ Maximum drift velocity (0 = disabled)
+   XJ      = 0.2u       $ Junction depth
+   LD      = 0.05u      $ Lateral diffusion
+   DELTA   = 0.5        $ Narrow-width factor
+   NFS     = 1e11       $ Fast surface state density
+   TPG     = 1          $ Gate material (+1 = n+ poly)
+   TOX     = 100n       $ Gate oxide thickness (normalised)
+   NSUB    = 4e15       $ Substrate doping (cm⁻³)
+   UO      = 600        $ Surface mobility (cm²/V·s), reduced for power MOSFET
+   RD      = 0          $ Drain ohmic resistance (handled externally)
+   RS      = 0          $ Source ohmic resistance (handled externally)
+   RG      = 0          $ Gate resistance (handled externally)
+   IS      = 1e-14      $ Bulk p-n saturation current
+   CGSO    = 1.1n       $ Gate-source overlap cap per unit W  (Ciss-Crss ≈ 2505pF → scaled)
+   CGDO    = 195p       $ Gate-drain overlap cap per unit W   (Crss ≈ 195pF)
+   CGBO    = 10p        $ Gate-bulk overlap cap per unit length
+   CJ      = 500u       $ Zero-bias bulk junction cap (F/m²) — Coss contribution
+   CJSW    = 10n        $ Sidewall junction cap
+   MJ      = 0.5        $ Bulk junction grading coefficient
+   MJSW    = 0.33       $ Sidewall grading coefficient
+   PB      = 0.8        $ Bulk junction potential

* ---------------------------------------------------------------
* Body (anti-parallel) diode
*   Forward drop  ≈ 1.5 V at IS=25A  (VSD = 1.5V typ from datasheet)
*   Reverse recovery trr = 136 ns
*   CJO set to reproduce Coss at low VDS
* ---------------------------------------------------------------

Dbody  Si  Di  IRLZ44N_BODY

.MODEL IRLZ44N_BODY  D
+   IS    = 1.5e-11     $ Saturation current (tuned for Vf=1.5V at 25A)
+   N     = 1.05        $ Emission coefficient
+   RS    = 4m          $ Series resistance (Ω)
+   TT    = 136n        $ Transit time ≈ trr = 136 ns
+   CJO   = 810p        $ Zero-bias junction cap → Coss @ VDS≈0 (pF)
+   VJ    = 0.8         $ Junction built-in potential (V)
+   M     = 0.45        $ Grading coefficient
+   EG    = 1.11        $ Energy gap (Si)
+   XTI   = 3.0         $ Saturation current temp exponent
+   BV    = 55          $ Reverse breakdown = VDSS (V)
+   IBV   = 1m          $ Current at BV (A)

.ENDS IRLZ44N

*==============================================================================
* USAGE EXAMPLE:
*
*   X1  VD  VG  VS  IRLZ44N
*
* where VD = drain node, VG = gate node, VS = source node.
*
* The subcircuit models:
*   - Channel conduction (Level-3 MOSFET)
*   - Gate, drain and source parasitic resistances
*   - Body diode with reverse-recovery (TT parameter)
*   - Nonlinear capacitances Ciss, Coss, Crss via MOSFET + diode model
*
* NOTE:
*   This model is derived from the datasheet parameters. For best accuracy
*   at a specific operating point, KP, VTO, and THETA may need fine-tuning
*   against the VGS vs ID transfer curves (Figure 3 in the datasheet).
*   Thermal effects are not modelled; for power-dissipation simulations
*   use an external thermal RC network (RθJC=0.80°C/W, RθJA=62°C/W).
*==============================================================================
